sequenceDiagram
    title BinaryPipe Lifecycle: Available, Transfer, Unavailable

    participant Product as Product
    participant CN as CN<br>[implements BinaryPipeSend,<br>BinaryPipeReceive]

    rect rgb(230, 230, 240)
        note over Product, CN: 1. Connection available
        CN-->>Product: BinaryPipeConnection.Available()

        Note over Product: BinaryPipe is ready for data transfer.<br>Send/Receive operations can now be used.
    end

    rect rgb(230, 230, 240)
        note over Product, CN: 2. Send data
        Product->>CN: BinaryPipeSend.SendData(<br>subchannel=1, data=256 bytes)
        CN-->>Product: BinaryPipeSendResponse.SendCompleted()

        Product->>CN: BinaryPipeSend.SendData(<br>subchannel=1, data=256 bytes)
        CN-->>Product: BinaryPipeSendResponse.SendCompleted()
    end

    rect rgb(230, 230, 240)
        note over Product, CN: 3. Receive data
        Product->>CN: BinaryPipeReceive.ReceiveData(<br>subchannel=1, report=true)
        CN-->>Product: BinaryPipeReceiveResponse.DataReceived(<br>subchannel=1, data=256 bytes)
        CN-->>Product: BinaryPipeReceiveResponse.DataReceived(<br>subchannel=1, data=256 bytes)
    end

    rect rgb(230, 230, 240)
        note over Product, CN: 4. Connection lost
        CN-->>Product: BinaryPipeConnection.Unavailable()
        CN-->>Product: GapCentralResponse.CurrentState(standby)

        Note over Product: No further Send/Receive operations until<br>a new connection and Available() is received.
    end
